{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-categorical-connection-exists","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proof","doco:Section"],"label":"prf:categorical-connection-exists","kind":"proof","title":"Proof of existence of categorical connections","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-connection-exists"],"text":"categorical-connection-exists-proof.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prf:categorical-connection-exists\"></a><p>Witness: the trivial connection <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\nabla_0 = d</code>, where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d</code> is the\nde Rham differential of the Kähler module <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Omega^1(A)</code>.  The\nLeibniz rule <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d(ab) = (da)b + a(db)</code> is part of the differential-\ncalculus axiom of the QU.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-connection-exists-proof.md","heading":"Proof"}
